   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate adaptation, mitigation, environment and biodiversity</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Expanding WASH Services in Mozambique - Australia Assists deployed a WASH Specialist with UNICEF to Pemba, Mozambique, The deployee supported co-ordination, management and reporting requirements for the WASH component of the Northern Crisis Recovery Project, which aimed to improve access to basic services and economic opportunities for internally displaced persons and host communities. The deployment contributed to the recruitment and capacity building of 300 temporary WASH facilitators; professional development for 130 people; temporary WASH to 33,000 IDPs and host communities; and durable water supply, sanitation and hygiene services in communities for 50,000 persons via the successful construction of water infrastructure components in 23 sites.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food security</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kiribati:
&#x200d;
In 2022-23 the Australia Assists program deployed a Disaster Risk Management and Response Coordination Specialist to the Office of the President, Kiribati. The Specialist worked closely with the National Drought Committee to review and update the national drought response and communication plans, including to expand the gathering and sharing of data across government ministries and support the coordination of water management plans and distribution points. This assisted with the improvement of Kiribati&#x2019;s national drought planning and response.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Samoa: 
&#x200d;
The Australia Assists program deployed a COVID-19 Recovery Specialist to support Samoa&#x2019;s National Disaster Management Office (NDMO) with an After-Action Review of Samoa&#x2019;s national COVID-19 response. As a result of this support, the NDMO was able to draw on the Review Report to inform amendments to Samoa&#x2019;s national disaster management policy and planning to strengthen health systems resilience to future health emergencies.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening midwifery care in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar - Australia Assists deployed a Clinical Nurse to UNFPA to improve neonatal and maternal care within Rohingya refugee camps and host communities in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar. The deployee trained 495 midwives (including 25 midwife supervisors) in live-saving emergency obstetrics care training, focussed on the primary causes of maternal mortality among Rohingya refugees, including breech and shoulder deliveries; post-partum haemorrhage; sepsis management; neonatal resuscitation and infection prevention. The deployee worked across nine primary healthcare facilities and two secondary healthcare facilities, and provided one-on-one mentoring to 38 midwives. Additionally, the deployee developed a booklet outlining good practice to reinforce skills developed during training, to be utilised by all UNFPA partners.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate adaptation, mitigation, environment and biodiversity</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting green energy transition in Iraq - Australia Assists deployed a Renewable Energy Climate Mitigation Specialist to UNDP in Baghdad, Iraq. The deployee supported Iraqi delegates to COP28 through training on renewable energy, energy transition and energy efficiency. The deployee also supported broader work on renewable energy and energy efficiency, including conducting a needs analysis, and reviewing strategies to promote investments in this sector. Through the deployment, concept notes were developed on options for the Iraqi renewable and green energy sectors, aligning with global requirements, particularly in response to climate change issues worldwide.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting programming in HIV/AIDS and prevention of violence against women and girls in Southern Africa - Australia Assists deployed a Programme Specialist to UN Women, South Africa, to support finalisation of the Turning the Tide program, a program working towards ending violence against women and girls and HIV&amp;AIDS. The deployment prepared a detailed proposal for the program, including budget, workplan, and theory of change. This proposal will be used to raise awareness of the program with stakeholders and seek funding for delivery in Eswatini and Lesotho.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2023-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2024-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
